                                                "sense_id": "263c9c6a-a13f-3c9e-8310-5a6c51faa3c5",
                                                "text": "Fig. 16 is the striped or cucumber-bug, as it is improperly called, but which is in reality a beetle, while fig. 17, the squash-bug, is a true bug, being without jaws or mouth, except a long slender tube, fitted for piercing and sucking the sap of plants."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
